    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Find the Sundays",
        "body": "Sundays are $7$ apart, so they alternate odd and even. To have three even Sundays the month needs five Sundays starting on an even date; since a month has at most $31$ days, the first Sunday is the $2$nd ($4$ would put the fifth Sunday on the $32$nd). Sundays: $2, 9, 16, 23, 30$. The $10$th is the day after Sunday the $9$th: Monday.\n\n**Answer: (C) Monday**"
