    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Use coordinates",
        "body": "Put the left end of the top edge at $(0, 0)$ with $y$ measured downward. The outer edge runs right $40$ to $(40, 0)$, down $10$ to $(40, 10)$, right to $(60, 10)$ and down $30$ to $(60, 40)$. The inner edge, $5$ m away, runs along $y = 5$ to $x = 35$, down to $y = 15$, right $20$ m to $x = 55$, then down.\n\nThe yellow line is halfway between, $2.5$ m from each edge:\n\n- along $y = 2.5$ from $x = 0$ to $x = 37.5$: $37.5$ m\n- down $x = 37.5$ from $y = 2.5$ to $y = 12.5$: $10$ m\n- along $y = 12.5$ from $x = 37.5$ to $x = 57.5$: $20$ m\n- down $x = 57.5$ from $y = 12.5$ to $y = 40$: $27.5$ m\n\nTotal: $37.5 + 10 + 20 + 27.5 = 95$ m.\n\n**Answer: (C) 95 m**"
      }
