        "text": "$J$ and $T$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Each region has area 12",
        "body": "The grid has area $36$, so each region has area $12$. One line goes from $P$ to a point on the top edge, cutting off a right triangle with height $6$ (the left side). For area $12$ its base must be $4$: $\\frac12 \\times 6 \\times 4 = 12$. That is point $T$. By symmetry, the other line goes to the point on the right side $4$ units up: $J$. The middle region then has area $36 - 24 = 12$ too.\n\n**Answer: (E) $J$ and $T$**"
      }
