        "key": "C",
        "text": "15"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "0"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Pythagoras for the slanted sides",
        "body": "$F$, $S$, $G$ lie on a vertical line and $SR$ is horizontal, so $FG = 5 + 9 = 14$, $FR = \\sqrt{5^2 + 12^2} = 13$ and $GR = \\sqrt{9^2 + 12^2} = 15$.\n\n- (i) $13 + 12 + 9 = 34$\n- (ii) $5 + 9 + 15 = 29$\n- (iii) $13 + 15 + 9 = 37$\n- (iv) $5 + 12 + 15 = 32$\n\nLongest minus shortest: $37 - 29 = 8$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 8**"
      }
    ],
