        "key": "D",
        "text": "66"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "67"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Remove the extra chip",
        "body": "If $n$ cookies each had $k$ chips, plus one extra chip, then $nk + 1 = 1000$, so $nk = 999 = 3^3 \\times 37$. The divisors of $999$ are $1, 3, 9, 27, 37, 111, 333, 999$; the only one between $12$ and $36$ is $n = 27$, giving $k = 37$. The special cookie has $38$ chips, and $27 + 38 = 65$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 65**"
      }
    ],
